{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"qaoa-regularization","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:3206447b7c5ce37e42a253ccbbdf9ea9fd64af6c402a7a116e30915fbcfcd2a4/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618","passage_ref":"sha256:fa472c25832b36a2061f212196277009f716c230a658520bb4b4f2ed8173d74b/papers/long.md/sha256:3206447b7c5ce37e42a253ccbbdf9ea9fd64af6c402a7a116e30915fbcfcd2a4/papers/long.json/passages/qaoa-regularization","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&paper=long&passage=qaoa-regularization","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&paper=long&passage=qaoa-regularization","span":{"end_byte":134709,"end_line":3035,"start_byte":123860,"start_line":2832},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&view=arguments&node=circuit.sign_smoothing&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&node=circuit.sign_smoothing&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&node=circuit.sign_smoothing&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&view=arguments&node=circuit.sign_smoothing&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&ref=sha256%3A47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd%2Fnodes%2Fcircuit.sign_smoothing","record":{"assumption_ids":["scalar.paper_minimizer"],"boundary":"The order is terminal cutoff, finite scalar mesh, then finite smoothing. The statement has no joint-limit or uniform-in-terminal-time rate and still allows unbounded intermediate columns.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-sign-smoothing"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.sign_smoothing","kind":"claim","label":"Finite sign smoothing preserves the rooted value","locator":"03-classical-optimization.tex:220–254; eq:energy-l2-continuity, eq:scalar-near-optimal-smooth","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-qaoa-scalar","statement":"For a given minimizer, choose T<1 and then a sufficiently fine finite mesh N. At that fixed T,N, replace F_N=sgn(H_N) by tanh(kH_N). The independent final uniform-rounding coordinate gives P(H_N=0)=0, so this converges in L² as k→∞. For every error>0, finite T,N,k give a centered finite descendant output z with |z|≤1 and E(z)≥P_*−error; local maps are odd and smooth with polynomially bounded derivatives.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.sign_smoothing","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.sign_smoothing","id":"field:ea1474919cf23af481e893086c043ed79436aac7fa61e78365b3d48ed9a9216a","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.sign_smoothing","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.paper_minimizer"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer%22%2C%22circuit.sign_smoothing%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.class